e middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and July to August and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 156% of normal in May to June but only 45% in September to October. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 46% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2005, with grid 15439 at 47% that year.</p>"}
